# Build vs deploy separation

## Build (Phases 1–4)

- Phase 1 discovery gate: see `AGENTS.md`, `SKILLS.md`, and `/onboard-workflow`.
- Sub-agents (`prompts/onboarding/01-*.md` … `04-*.md`) **never** call AWS, MCP, or Terraform.
- Allowed: write under `workloads/{name}/`, run `pytest`, `validate_configs.py`, `validate_compute.py`, `render_workload.py`.
- **Do not** Write/Edit `workloads/*/scripts/**` or `orchestration/*_state_machine.json` directly — `.cursor/hooks.json` and `.claude/settings.json` block agent writes; use codegen specs + renderer.
- Stop after tests pass and present artifacts for human approval.

## Deploy (Phase 5)

- **Main agent only**, and only after the user explicitly requests deploy.
- Read `docs/MCP_GUARDRAILS.md` — MCP-first catalog/LF/verify; Terraform fallback for jobs/SFN.
- Preflight: `python tools/deploy_workload.py --workload {name} --dry-run`
- Live plan: `python tools/deploy_workload.py --workload {name} --bucket {bucket}`
- `terraform apply` requires `--approve-apply` **and** user confirmation in chat.
- Wrapper refuses apply if `terraform_sync.status=pending` or no `module "{name}"` in `main.tf`.
- Record successful SFN execution in `docs/STATUS.md`.
- Append phases to `workloads/{name}/logs/trace_events.jsonl` via `shared.utils.agent_trace`.

## Command entry points

`.cursor/commands/onboard-workflow.md` — build.
`.cursor/commands/devops-workflow.md` — Terraform + plan after onboard.
Tool selection: `TOOL_ROUTING.md`.
